// Real NFL coaching staffs for Franchise mode: every team's head coach, offensive coordinator and defensive
// coordinator for the 2026 season as of 2026-11-13, plus a market of coaches who are out of the league.
// GENERATED by F:\bap-agents\coaches\compute.py from pages fetched that day. Do not hand-edit the numbers: change
// the inputs there and rebuild. Per-coach evidence is in F:\bap-agents\coaches\notes.json, the page each job was
// read from in sources.csv.
//
// WHO HOLDS EACH JOB
//   Each of the 96 names was read from the team's own coaching-staff page (fetched 2026-11-13) and matched against
//   Wikipedia's lists of current head coaches / offensive / defensive coordinators; the 32 head coaches also against
//   ESPN's 2026 team coach records. In-season changes through that date: Carolina fired Ejiro Evero in late October
//   (Todd Wash is the interim, `interim: true`); Sean Payton took play-calling back from Davis Webb and DeMeco Ryans
//   took it from Matt Burke before Week 5. No head coach has been fired this season.
//   Tampa Bay has no defensive coordinator (Todd Bowles runs the defense). Its row is George Edwards, the defensive
//   pass game coordinator and a former NFL coordinator; `title` carries his real title.
//   `calls`: ESPN's "Who calls plays for every NFL team in 2026" (September) and ran.de's staff list of October 30.
//   `age` on 2026-11-13 from the birth date on his Wikipedia page (null where it has none); `since` = first season
//   in this job with this team.
//
// RATINGS, 0-11 (0 F, 1 D, 3 C, 6 B, 9 A, 11 S), each one a formula over public results, not an opinion.
//   Inputs: every NFL game 1999-2026 (ESPN scoreboards) and ESPN team statistics 2004-2026, turned into one row per
//   team-season; each coach's seasons as head coach / OC / DC from his Wikipedia career list. A unit's level in a
//   season is a z-score against the league: 60% points per game, 40% yards per play (points only before 2004).
//   Seasons are weighted 0.90 per year back from 2026; the season in progress counts 60% of its games played.
//   Every average is pulled toward a prior by a fixed number of phantom seasons, so a short record stays near the
//   middle: a first-year or interim coach sits just under average until he has a record.
//   offPlaycalling / defPlaycalling: the level of his units in the seasons he was that side's coordinator or a head
//     coach from that side. Full credit when he called the plays; half weight and 60% of the result when a head coach
//     called them over him (70% for a head coach who left the calls to his coordinator). Prior: 2 seasons at -0.2.
//     Rating = 5.5 + 7 x z above average, 5.5 + 5.5 x z below it. A head coach who has never called plays tops out
//     at 8 on his own side. The other side for a head coach is "his units under him": 4 + 3 x z, kept within 2-7.
//     A coordinator with no record on the other side gets 2.
//   talentDev: how far his units (a head coach: his team's two units) stood above half the level he inherited, over
//     each stint (half weight for a coordinator's seasons under a play-calling head coach): 5 + 5.5 x that lift
//     (prior 3 seasons at 0); 4 with no record. A few carry a +1 with the reason
//     in notes.json (players who became All-Pros or MVPs under him).
//   culture: winning that lasts. Shrunk win percentage in his seasons as a head coach (seasons as a coordinator at
//     30%), playoff appearance rate, and for a sitting head coach up to +1 for tenure (a tenth of a point a year).
//   situational: record in one-score games (8 points or fewer), wins above what his point differential predicts,
//     fourth-down attempts against what his record predicts, and his side's third-down rate. A coordinator who has
//     never been a head coach is rated on third downs alone.
//   What the numbers cannot see: fourth-down decision grades and challenge records are not public in a form that
//     could be fetched, Pro Football Reference refused the request, and mid-season firings are credited as whole
//     seasons. College records count only as a stated prior (notes.json).
//
// OVR, 0-99 = round(46 + 5.1 x c), where
//   head coach:   c = 0.26 culture + 0.22 situational + 0.18 talentDev + 0.24 (his better play-calling side) + 0.10 (the other)
//   coordinator:  c = 0.50 his own side's play-calling + 0.20 talentDev + 0.15 situational + 0.10 culture + 0.05 the other side
//
// Row shape: { name, team, role: 'HC' | 'OC' | 'DC', age, since, calls, side?, interim?, title?, attrs, ovr }
//   calls: head coach = the side he calls himself ('off' | 'def' | null); coordinator = true when he is the play-caller.
//   side:  head coaches only, his background ('off' | 'def' | 'st').
//   COACH_FREE_AGENTS: same shape, team null, role = the job he fits best. Each is on no team's staff page and his
//   Wikipedia page lists no current team as of 2026-11-13 (several work in television).

export const COACH_TYPES = ['talentDev', 'offPlaycalling', 'defPlaycalling', 'culture', 'situational']

